      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There was a bit of a mess with the Avatars 3.0 release where it looks like they fixed a long standing issue for some vr controllers of the alignment being incorrect. Then for some reason, I think it was for vive controls, they reversed the fix. As of recently I have not noticed any major changes but the alignment has never been good.\nI can say though I am getting very annoyed at how the controller placement is so far offset from the wrist. On my main avatar it puts my oculus controller up by the tips of the fingers and nowhere near the wrist bone.\nThere appear to be two problems here with the alignment, rotation and position. Position I believe has been offset to assist in IK limits or just for calibration purposes, but without customisation from the user it wont fit every avatar. The rotation is an odd one because they had it fixed during the initial release of AV3.0 and I am confused as to why the changes were reverted or not given as a choice to toggle.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-13T20:51:24.012Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've noticed that in a lot of avatars the hand alignemt isn't really proper, this might have been done accidentally in an update and has flown under the radar for more than enough already. There was another post that talked about this https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/avatar-hands-broke-after-update but didn't really get much attention.\nBetter hand alignment please?",
